<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suessa Aurunca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sessa Aurunca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suessa Aurunca was a town of the Aurunci in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, now Sessa Aurunca. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> destroyed the Aurunci in the later fourth century BCE, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> colony was founded there in 313 BCE. It remained a prosperous Roman town on the edge of the Ager Falernus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suessa-aurunca.jpg" alt="Suessa Aurunca" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gianni Bencivenga · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sessa_Aurunca_-_veduta_aerea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
